/P 51 0 R
/E (The International Monetary Fund \(IMF\) has a role in fixing global money problems and helping countries that are in financial trouble. The IMF was created in 1944. Its job is to bring together countries so they can work together on money matters and keep the global financial system stable. The IMF watches how economies are doing. They provide funds and tell governments what to do to keep the economy healthy.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 51 0 R
/E (A key job of the IMF is to give money help to countries that are in a crisis. If a country has accumulated alot debt, low foreign currency reserves or cannot pay for important imports it can ask the IMF for help. This help is meant to bring the economy to a stable state restore confidence and let governments fix the deeper problems. The IMF usually asks for certain policy steps that the governments must follow.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
