/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Even though these rules are meant to bring stability people around the world have started to argue about how they affect everyday life. Some changes put strain on people who already struggle with higher prices, jobs that are hard to find and not enough basic services. For instance cutting government subsidies can make everyday goods cost more. That can make public anger rise.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (So the IMFs role is to bring back economic steadiness but it also must make sure its rules do not hurt the most vulnerable. Protecting spending making safety nets stronger and thinking about how reforms affect society are all key parts of the job)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
