>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (However, achieving this balance remains complex. Governments must address financial difficulties while continuing to provide essential services and support their populations. Economic reforms that fail to consider the needs of citizens may contribute to public dissatisfaction and weaken trust in institutions.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (Therefore, effective cooperation between the IMF, national governments and other international organizations is essential. By considering the socioeconomic consequences of financial policies, countries can work toward economic recovery while reducing the risk of worsening public unrest.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
105 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 53 0 R
/T (Challenges and Controversies)
/E (Challenges and Controversies)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
106 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (Despite its role in promoting international financial stability, the IMF has faced criticism regarding the effects of its economic programmes. One major concern is whether the conditions attached to financial assistance can place excessive pressure on populations already experiencing economic hardship. Critics argue that certain reforms may prioritize financial stability over social welfare, while supporters emphasize the importance of addressing underlying economic problems to achieve sustainable recovery.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
