>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Another significant challenge is balancing international financial assistance with national sovereignty. Although countries voluntarily request IMF assistance, the conditions attached to these programmes may influence domestic economic policies. This raises questions about the extent to which governments should be expected to implement international recommendations while maintaining their responsibility toward their citizens.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 54 0 R
/E (Furthermore, the IMF cannot independently resolve every cause of public unrest. Economic instability is often connected to broader issues such as corruption, inequality, weak institutions and political dissatisfaction. Addressing these challenges requires cooperation between national governments, international financial institutions and the wider international community.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
